WEBVTT

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.190
<b>Vladivostok, Russia</b>

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.830
Who's there?!

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:41.080
Are you in charge of Vladivostok?

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:45.100
Indeed. Let's hear your name.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.110
Haimura Moroha.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:53.110
It's you...

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.590
Where's the Lightning Emperor?

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.610
Then you shall test my loyalty!

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:12.190
Not bad. But my barrier has the approval 
of the Lightning Emperor herself.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.430
I remember!

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:26.660
Write!

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.430
<b>Dance, dance, spear of the lightning god.</b>

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.110
What?!

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:31.690
No!

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:36.690
<b>Come thunder, come rumbling. None of this world lives forever.</b>

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:36.700
Stop chanting! Don't tarnish 
our lord's sacred land!

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.810
<b>Ephemeral sparkles, embrace pleasure. It is the banquet of killing.</b>

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.660
Thunderstorm Helix!

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.530
Did you kill him?

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:55.530
Of course not.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:59.050
I'm not killing anyone in this war.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.460
A fake passport and a fake visa.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.150
I wouldn't expect less from UK Headquarters.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:04:00.760
Damn it, why do I have to be away from 
Edward-sama to take care of this kid?

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.220
Please don't say that.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.360
Edward-sama is no better,

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.840
cooperating with a personal war 
against the Russian headquarters.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.910
What if this becomes public?

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:15.830
That's why I don't want you 
to be involved, Angela-san.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.380
You don't have to tell me that.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:26.200
So, what do you mean by you won't 
be killing anyone in this war?

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.990
It means exactly what it sounds like.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:39.780
Unfortunately for you, I don't know 
where the Lightning Emperor is.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:41.850
I thought you'd say so.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:42.510
What?

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:47.440
Don't you want to inform the Lightning 
Emperor that I'm here to wage war?

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:50.020
Hey, what the heck are you thinking?

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.070
I'm going to be talking to 
the Khabarovsk leader next.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.840
You could inform her on that, too.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.180
Wait, wait.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.410
You're here to wage war, aren't you?

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.260
Why would you give the enemy information?

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:05.870
I don't want to waste time taking 
prisoners or interrogating people.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.690
You Japanese people sure are naïve.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.250
One can't be blamed for accusing you 
of having gone senile from the peace.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.790
Hey, he's mocking you, Haimura.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:19.850
Naïve, huh?

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.260
Y-You...

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.490
Do you have dreams about your past life?

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.530
And do you remember them?

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.850
Of course, why would you even ask?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:38.850
I do, too.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:44.360
I'm always standing alone on the 
battlefield, fighting countless enemies.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:05:59.730
Japanese people are naïve?

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.170
Senile from the peace?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:04.160
What the hell are you talking about?

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:13.440
Wait...

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.890
Let's go, then.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.450
Hey, wait. Haimura!

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:23.690
He's a Rank A Russian.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.830
That won't kill him.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:31.340
That may be, but isn't the Lightning 
Emperor who you're really after?

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:32.790
It's simple.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.300
Neither Edward's intel nor interrogating 
district leaders will tell me

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.380
where the Lightning Emperor is.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.170
So I just have to wreck all the 
district leaders, one by one.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.630
Then the Lightning Emperor 
will have to mobilize.

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:55.480
But it'll be a nuisance if the others 
meet up and start another battle.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:59.980
Well, I don't think we'll run into any 
other people from the Russian Branch.

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.900
Apparently they'd be disciplined 
immediately if they mess up.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.270
I hope so.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:10.680
Their loyalty to the Lightning 
Emperor is extreme.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.670
What if they inform the Lightning 
Emperor accepting that they'll die?

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:27.110
That's not completely implausible,

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:31.130
but that's exactly why I don't 
want to kill anyone in this war.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:33.660
It's not because you're naïve?

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.420
No, it's better that way for sure.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.530
You'll understand soon.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:41.480
Jack-in-the-box.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:47.020
You really are a man full of surprises.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:57.030
Raise your head, Bernard.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.540
I forgive you.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.160
Skip the greetings.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:09.830
State your purpose.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.510
I am sleepy.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.610
I... I was defeated by Haimura!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.360
And?

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:21.960
O-Ordinarily I would ought to kill myself.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.970
However, if I am to die either way, 
I would like to take Haimura with me.

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:26.760
That must not be.

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:31.030
I do not accept failure.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:32.540
Die.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:34.700
Then one more thing!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.750
You're persistent.

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:40.350
Haimura couldn't kill me 
with his Thunderstorm Helix.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:50.160
Did you hear that, people?

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.000
You are impressive indeed.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.370
I know your loyalty well.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:59.600
I will make good use of your life.

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:02.030
I am deeply grateful.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.180
Yes, noble.

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:08.680
<b>Dance, dance, dragon of lightning bolts.</b>

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.680
<b>Bring forth the blue lightning.</b>

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:13.680
<b>None of this world live forever. Ephemeral sparkles, 
embrace pleasure. Destroy all in the blink of an eye.</b>

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.690
<b>Do not regret being late, it is the banquet of killing.</b>

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.320
Thunderbolt Dragon!

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.190
S-See that, Haimura?

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:41.710
This is the true might 
of the Lightning Emperor.

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:44.480
You'll never come close!

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:47.430
This is true pleasure.

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:48.230
True pleasure.

00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:49.230
True pleasure.

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.150
Long live the Lightning Emperor!

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.020
<i>What a foolish man.</i>

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:13.420
According to Bernard, Haimura intends 
to destroy Khabarovsk next.

00:10:13.850 --> 00:10:15.360
What shall we do?

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:17.510
We needn't do anything.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.270
What?

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:24.390
Instead, the people here should, say, 
reinforce defenses around Krasnoyarsk.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:28.880
You're going to abandon 
everything east of Siberia?

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:33.710
They wouldn't be able to surround 
Haimura if I asked them to do it now.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:37.180
I see, that is impressive, Lightning Emperor!

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:39.330
An astute decision!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:46.690
I don't care who, I hope someone 
will at least take an arm with them.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:59.220
Uh, are we seriously going to be here 
in this cramped room, just the two of us?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:04.140
Oh dear, does Moroha-chan have trouble 
sleeping without his favorite pillow?

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:06.880
Shall I hold you, then?

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:07.950
Oh, really?

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:10.770
Why thank you, then.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.980
Hey, kid! I wasn't serious, you pervert!

00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:17.430
Don't you dare cross this line!

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:18.810
I'll kill you if you do.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.760
How do we get changed?

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.620
We'll both face the other 
way and plug our ears!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:26.070
I'll kill you if you look or try to listen.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.370
Understood, I'll be careful.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.350
Yeah, it's fine.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.430
Did you not hear me?

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.500
I said I'm going to become 
Moroha's younger sister.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:25.680
<i>I-I'm</i> Moroha's younger sister, past, present 
and future lives, forever! Only me!

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:30.140
Moroha told me he would be my family.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:35.350
Then you can at least be his older sister!

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.610
No, I want to be his younger sister.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:43.900
How can you two keep fighting 
over something so silly?

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.820
It's not silly!

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.360
It's a serious matter of identity!

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.660
Is it really about identity?

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.760
Urushibara Shizuno.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.950
I want you to help me.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:59.410
I want you to explain to 
this blockhead for me.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:02.180
Why would I bother?

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.040
See!

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:08.650
Urushibara is on my side!

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.120
I'm depressed. Time to die.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:14.770
You both ought to stop this silly fight.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.370
I think Moroha would be disappointed

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:19.820
if he saw you both in a foul 
mood when he gets back.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:24.500
Moroha is at war all by himself right now.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.330
So...

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.490
Sorry.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.850
You look like you're getting along well.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.750
For Nii-sama's sake, yeah.

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:01.330
I wonder how Nii-sama's doing 
right about now, though.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:04.320
Yes.

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:11.110
His body pillow is lonely 
sleeping alone these days.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:14.360
Please survive.

00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:18.080
Please show me your smile once more.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:19.840
Of course he will.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.290
My Nii-sama would never lose.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:23.720
Never.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:24.980
Yeah.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.350
<b>Khabarovsk</b>

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:34.770
Haimura Moroha.

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:36.770
Remember that.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.690
That's the name of the man who defeated you.

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.770
<b>Khabarovsk Branch Neutralized</b>

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:47.650
Khabarovsk

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.490
Chita

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.490
Ulan-Ude

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.490
<b>Chita Branch Neutralized</b>

00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:01.470
Ed-sama, your necktie is crooked again.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.390
Silly you.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.670
Chita

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.670
Ulan-Ude

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.670
Irkutsk

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.850
<b>Ulan-Ude Branch Neutralized</b>

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.060
Irkutsk                      Ulan-Ude

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.060
Chita

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:25.690
Freezing Shade!

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:31.990
<b>Irkutsk Branch Neutralized</b>

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.490
Krasnoyarsk

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.490
Irkutsk

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.500
<b>Krasnoyarsk Station</b>

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:49.820
Have you noticed?

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:51.560
There're eight of them.

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:54.160
Isn't it seven?

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:56.010
No, eight.

00:15:57.110 --> 00:15:58.790
Don't blame me.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.560
This is all your doing.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.560
I know.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.990
Is there anywhere we can really fight,

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:06.020
without restraint and 
without causing anyone trouble?

00:16:08.240 --> 00:16:10.230
Are you calling someone again?

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.430
What do you mean, "again"?

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.380
I'm not calling anyone.

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:17.000
It's a little far, but there's a large grove.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.780
I'll go check it out.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.390
Alone? really?

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:25.800
Take care of my luggage, please.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:32.470
Hey, I'm not your bellboy!

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:39.620
<i>They're following me.</i>

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:50.590
Why don't you show your faces already?

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:09.840
I'm the Krasnoyarsk district leader, 
Kirsan Romanovich Pavlyuchenko.

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:11.930
Haimura Moroha.

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:17.360
You must have realized that the 
leaders of each district—

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:21.040
all Rank A—have surrounded you.

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.050
What of it?

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.770
I won't ask you to surrender.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.290
Just go back to Japan in peace!

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:33.610
If we fight, the majority of 
us will end up dead with you.

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:36.550
We can't go against the 
Lightning Emperor's commands,

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.660
but we don't want to fight 
you if we can avoid it!

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.790
That's enough, Kirsan.

00:17:42.110 --> 00:17:45.640
The Lightning Emperor's order 
is to slay that monster.

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.650
No exceptions.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.610
For the Lightning Emperor!

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.380
Come, Saratiga!

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:02.920
<i>Freezing Shade!</i>

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.020
<i>I need to find somewhere open.</i>

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:13.240
Shadow clones!

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.060
Die, Haimura!

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:16.820
For Bernard-sama!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.780
No, twins!

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:19.980
Then...

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:20.740
How about this!

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:31.590
You!

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:35.870
Die, die, die!

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:38.590
You'll pay for killing Bernard-sama!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:41.250
Said who?

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:43.100
The Lightning Lord!

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.150
That's a false charge!

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:48.730
They'll hit their friendlies!

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:50.450
Now die!

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.000
Idiots, you're going to 
be the ones who'll die!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.650
Hot!

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:09.370
I hope those twins are safe.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:21.340
Poison gas.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:28.730
Breeze Blade!

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.150
One down.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.240
So they lured me in.

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.830
I won't fall for that twice!

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:51.750
Decree's Weight!

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.710
Is this your first time in aerial combat?

00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.940
Die!

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:03.220
<b>Shapeless blade, slaying the invisible, come,</b>

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:04.850
Freeze Blade!

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:09.710
Spirit of ice and snow...

00:20:17.280 --> 00:20:18.530
That's four.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:20.280
Now...

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:23.740
there's one more over there.

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:27.490
I noticed you.

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:33.240
You went easy on me with your 
Freezing Shade, didn't you?

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:35.930
Why?

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:40.980
Y-You saved the twins, too.

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.250
Why?

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.410
No one wants to die.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:58.020
Yeah, you're right.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.260
Haimura!

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.990
Tell them I defeated you.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:10.600
By a flick to the forehead?

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.710
You won't get away!

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.160
Bernard-sama's enemy!

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:17.460
I told you, I didn't kill him.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:22.090
Seven down.

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:25.090
And...

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:28.100
Damn, so there really were eight.

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.060
Angela-san?!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:37.630
What are you doing?

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:39.730
I'm not your bellboy.

00:21:40.390 --> 00:21:42.230
That one's mine.

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.490
<b>Die, die, die, die.</b>

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:48.490
<b>All life must perish. Deliverance of the soul is simple.</b>

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:52.490
<b>Remove your heavy clothes and share with all 
the comfort of journeying heaven and earth.</b>

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:51.850
The Lightning Emperor.

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:52.490
Her?

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:56.500
<b>Oh, death, so sweet!</b>

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:58.000
<i>She finished chanting.</i>

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:07.130
Haimura!

00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:17.980
<i>Far away, in the great lands of Russia.</i>

00:22:18.550 --> 00:22:20.860
<i>I pray again, tonight.</i>

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:29.720
Haimura!

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:34.830
<i>May the wind blowing westward 
take our wishes with it.</i>

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:42.880
<i>That Moroha-san will be 
protected from all disasters.</i>

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:44.270
<i>That is all.</i>

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:24.770
